  "title": "Three single-formula handovers (TOH, QH, BTH) against the previous handover methods, with a teacher-free control",
  "framing": "Development experiment. DMOSpeech 2's teacher runs 3 steps and the student finishes; the three candidates differ only in what crosses (TOH: timing; QH: per-band time order with the student's values; BTH: timing from a teacher that never receives the prompt) and are applied to every input with no routing. Compared on the same cases with W4, W8, STAC, CH3 and CH3_LTT (thresholds fixed by earlier work) and with a teacher-free random re-timing (RND). Speakers have not been through TOH.",
