  "hypotheses": {
    "T1": "For each candidate X in TOH3, QH3, BTH3: clean pitch variety CVf0(X) - CVf0(RND), 95% bootstrap lower bound > 0 (the teacher adds variety beyond a random re-timing of the same size).",
    "T2": "For each candidate X: clean UTMOS(X) - UTMOS(RND), lower bound > 0 (the teacher's contribution sounds more natural than random re-timing).",
    "C": "For each candidate X: per-speaker mean over reverb03, reverb09 and babble15 of UTMOS(X) - UTMOS(W4), lower bound > 0 (X keeps recording conditions other than white noise out better than DMOSpeech 2's handover).",
    "M": "Candidate X beats a previous method C if, against C, (a) clean prompts: mean dUTMOS >= -0.08, dWER upper bound <= +0.01 and dSIM lower bound >= -0.01, and (b) the per-speaker mean over the five degraded conditions: dUTMOS lower bound > 0, dWER upper bound <= +0.01 and dSIM lower bound >= -0.01. Previous methods: W4, W8, STAC, CH3 and CH3_LTT."
  },
  "verdict_rule": "Per candidate X in TOH3, QH3 and BTH3, three labels: teacher = teacher_needed if T1 or T2 holds, else teacher_not_shown_needed; method = beats_all_previous if M holds against all five previous methods, beats_some_previous if against at least one, else beats_no_previous; condition = condition_safety_shown if C holds, else condition_safety_not_shown. partial if a stage is missing. Candidates are not ranked by the frozen rule; no correction for the three candidates (development pilot). Exploratory: contrasts between candidates (including aligned CVf0 QH3 - TOH3 and reverb/babble UTMOS BTH3 - TOH3), the SNR-routed methods SNR_TOH, SNR_W4 and SNR_RND, the first design's S1 (SNR_TOH - SNR_W4 on gated-in reverb and babble cases), STU against the previous methods, per-condition tables, aligned CVf0 and timing spread, BTH3's teacher sequence length, the EXP-030 replication, Definition 3.1 failures against W8, the policies' step choices, runaway outputs (WER > 1) and the EXP-011 reproduction.",
